  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1230 PM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nProminent ridging continues out west with the ridge axis over the \nRockies. That places us in northwest flow aloft with a couple of \nridge rider waves influencing our weather today and tomorrow. There \nis low to medium confidence on the potential for convection this \nafternoon through the early overnight. SPC does, however, have us in \na Slight Risk (level 2 of 5) for severe weather should this complex \nform, with damaging winds being the main threat. Models are \njuggling this evening's convection with most bringing an MCV \nthrough eastern portions of the CWA, while a few (such as the \n13Z HRRR) miss us just east. Best timing looks to be around 5PM \n- 10PM, though some convection may pop up as early as 19Z and \nmay linger as late as 11- 12Z tomorrow. Another wave tomorrow \nmay generate convection that models have mostly missing us to \nthe east. SPC has us in a Marginal Risk (level 1 of 5) for the \neastern half of the CWA, main threat is damaging winds again.\n\nWith regards to the heat...due to the lack of convection this \nmorning and dewpoints in the 80s, have expanded the Excessive Heat \nWarning east by a row of counties and run it through Tuesday. Have \nalso expanded the Heat Advisory to the remainder of the CWA for \nTuesday. Both regions now run from today through Tuesday. There is a \nlot of boundary layer moisture and subsequent high dewpoints through \nTuesday along with highs in the mid to upper 90s generally. Some of \nthis may be mitigated by convection at times. Some relief comes on \nWednesday onward with highs in the 80s, feeling more seasonable.",
